1. Which layer of the OSI model is responsible for routing?
a) Physical
b) Data Link
*c) Network
d) Transport

2. What device operates primarily at Layer 2 of the OSI model?
a) Router
*b) Switch
c) Firewall
d) Repeater

3. Which protocol is used for secure remote terminal access?
a) Telnet
*b) SSH
c) FTP
d) HTTP

4. What is the function of a proxy server?
a) To filter incoming traffic
b) To load balance requests
*c) To act as an intermediary for requests
d) To attach storage to the network

5. Which cloud deployment model allows infrastructure to be used by multiple organizations but is managed privately?
a) Public
b) Private
c) Hybrid
*d) Community

6. Which port is used by the Simple Mail Transfer Protocol (SMTP)?
a) 22
*b) 25
c) 53
d) 80

7. What type of IP address is 255.255.255.255?
a) Unicast
b) Multicast
*c) Broadcast
d) Anycast

8. What cable is characterized by a copper conductor surrounded by insulation and shielding, commonly used for broadband internet?
a) Fiber optic
*b) Coaxial
c) Twisted pair
d) Single-mode fiber

9. Which connector type is commonly used with twisted pair Ethernet cables?
a) SC
b) LC
*c) RJ-45
d) BNC

10. Which wireless standard operates in the 5 GHz band and provides higher data rates than 802.11b?
*a) 802.11a
b) 802.11b
c) 802.11g
d) 802.11n

11. Which network topology connects each device to a central device?
a) Mesh
*b) Star
c) Bus
d) Ring

12. In IPv4 addressing, which class supports 16-bit network portion and 16-bit host portion?
a) Class A
*b) Class B
c) Class C
d) Class D

13. What is the purpose of VLANs?
*a) To divide a physical network into logical subnets
b) To extend the wireless range
c) To provide physical security
d) To increase bandwidth

14. Which device provides functions like intrusion detection and prevention?
a) Load balancer
*b) IDS/IPS
c) Proxy server
d) Firewall

15. What is the role of the transport layer in the OSI model?
*a) Establishes, maintains, and terminates connections
b) Routes data between devices
c) Encrypts data
d) Defines the physical means of transmission

16. Which cloud service model provides hardware and networking resources but no middleware?
a) SaaS
b) PaaS
*c) IaaS
d) FaaS

17. Which Layer 1 technology allows multiple fibers to be pulled through a single connector?
*a) MPO
b) SC
c) LC
d) ST

18. What is the primary use of the TTL (Time to Live) field in an IP packet?
a) Control packet priority
*b) Limit packet lifespan to prevent routing loops
c) Encrypt data
d) Authenticate source

19. Which protocol is commonly used to automatically assign IP addresses?
a) DNS
*b) DHCP
c) FTP
d) SNMP

20. What type of traffic is sent to all devices in a subnet simultaneously?
a) Unicast
*b) Broadcast
c) Multicast
d) Anycast

21. Which protocol secures IP communications by authenticating and encrypting each IP packet?
a) GRE
*b) IPSec
c) TCP
d) UDP

22. Which wireless technology uses a star topology with a central controller managing access points?
a) Wi-Fi Ad hoc
*b) Infrastructure mode
c) Wired Equivalent Privacy
d) Mesh

23. Which cloud connectivity option provides a dedicated private connection between a customer and cloud provider?
a) VPN
*b) Direct Connect
c) NAT Gateway
d) Internet Gateway

24. Which network device balances incoming network traffic to optimize resource use?
a) Firewall
*b) Load balancer
c) IDS
d) Proxy

25. Which protocol is used to transfer files securely over a network using SSH?
a) FTP
*b) SFTP
c) TFTP
d) Telnet

26. Which of the following are valid IPv4 address classes?
[*] Class A
[*] Class B
[*] Class C
[ ] Class E

27. Which of the following are transmission media types?
[*] Coaxial cable
[*] 802.11 wireless
[*] Fiber optic
[ ] Bluetooth

28. Which protocols use port 22?
[*] SSH
[*] SFTP
[ ] Telnet
[ ] FTP

29. Which of these are cloud deployment models?
[*] Public
[*] Private
[*] Hybrid
[ ] Multi-cloud

30. Which of the following are functions of network appliances?
[*] Router
[*] NAS
[*] Firewall
[ ] VoIP Phone
